CORE
main.c

^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
subtype width times array size should be total bitvector width
^SIGNAL=6$
--
A struct with a bit-field followed by a flexible array member, hit by
memset, used to abort in bv_to_array_expr because the zero-length
flexible array member (int[0]) was handed the full struct bit-vector.
With the fix a zero-length array is allowed and reconstructed as an
empty array, so verification completes.
